---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const viteConfig = `// vite.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      '/__copypatch/api': {
        target: 'http://localhost:4040',
        changeOrigin: true,
        secure: false,
      },
    },
  },
});`;

const devScripts = `{
  "scripts": {
    "dev:site": "vite",
    "dev:server": "copypatch serve --port 4040 --db ./copypatch.sqlite --origin http://localhost:5173",
    "dev": "concurrently \"pnpm run dev:server\" \"pnpm run dev:site\"",
    "build": "tsc && vite build"
  }
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Vite & React Setup"
  description="How to configure Vite dev server proxy, concurrent development scripts, and production builds with CopyPatch."
>
  <h1>Vite & React Setup</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Integrating CopyPatch into a Vite + React application takes less than 2 minutes. By configuring a lightweight proxy in <code>vite.config.ts</code>, all API requests route directly to your CopyPatch backend under the same origin.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Configure Vite Proxy</h2>
  <p>
    Update <code>vite.config.ts</code> to forward <code>/__copypatch/api</code> calls to your local CopyPatch server:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={viteConfig} lang="typescript" title="vite.config.ts" />

  <h2>2. Concurrent Development Script</h2>
  <p>
    Add a unified dev command to your <code>package.json</code> using <code>concurrently</code>:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={devScripts} lang="json" title="package.json" />

  <h2>3. Start Developing</h2>
  <pre><code>pnpm install -D concurrently
pnpm run dev</code></pre>

  <p>
    Open <code>http://localhost:5173?copypatch=1</code> in your browser to unlock the editor!
  </p>

  <h2>Production Static Build</h2>
  <p>
    When running <code>vite build</code>, Vite compiles pure static HTML, CSS, and JS. The visitor bundle contains only the minimal <code>&lt;CopyPatchProvider&gt;</code> runtime (&lt; 1 kB gzip). The editor toolbar and auth modal are code-split into a separate chunk and only downloaded when <code>?copypatch=1</code> is requested.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
